<section id="A1" class="ltx_appendix">
<h2 class="ltx_title ltx_title_appendix"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_appendix">Appendix A </span>Proof and Derivation</h2>

<div id="A1.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A1.p1.1" class="ltx_p">In this section ,we proof the Proposition 3.1.</p>
</div>
<div id="A1.p2" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A1.p2.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A1.p2.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Definition</span> Given a Riemannian manifold <math id="A1.p2.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(M^{n},g)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>M</mi><mi>n</mi></msup><mo>,</mo><mi>g</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(M^{n},g)</annotation></semantics></math> and a function mapping <math id="A1.p2.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\varphi\in C^{\infty}(M)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>φ</mi><mo>∈</mo><mrow><msup><mi>C</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">∞</mi></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>M</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\varphi\in C^{\infty}(M)</annotation></semantics></math>, the differential map is linear for all <math id="A1.p2.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="x\in M" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo>∈</mo><mi>M</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">x\in M</annotation></semantics></math>. The gradient <math id="A1.p2.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\nabla_{g}\varphi" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mo>∇</mo><mi>g</mi></msub><mi>φ</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\nabla_{g}\varphi</annotation></semantics></math> of a function f is denoted as:</p>
<table id="A1.E12" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A1.E12.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\langle\nabla_{g}\varphi(x_{i}),X_{x_{i}}\rangle_{g(x)}=d_{x_{i}}\varphi(X_{x_{i}})" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">⟨</mo><mrow><mrow><mrow><msub><mo rspace="0.167em">∇</mo><mi>g</mi></msub><mi>φ</mi></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>X</mi><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">⟩</mo></mrow><mrow><mi>g</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></msub><mo>=</mo><mrow><msub><mi>d</mi><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>φ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>X</mi><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\langle\nabla_{g}\varphi(x_{i}),X_{x_{i}}\rangle_{g(x)}=d_{x_{i}}\varphi(X_{x_{i}})</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(12)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A1.p2.2" class="ltx_p">.</p>
</div>
<div id="A1.p3" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A1.p3.1" class="ltx_p">where <math id="A1.p3.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="d_{x_{i}}\varphi:T_{x_{i}}M\rightarrow\mathbb{R}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>d</mi><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>φ</mi></mrow><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>T</mi><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>M</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><mi>ℝ</mi></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">d_{x_{i}}\varphi:T_{x_{i}}M\rightarrow\mathbb{R}</annotation></semantics></math> is linear for all <math id="A1.p3.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="X_{x_{i}}\in T_{x_{i}}M" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>X</mi><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></msub><mo>∈</mo><mrow><msub><mi>T</mi><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>M</mi></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">X_{x_{i}}\in T_{x_{i}}M</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>
</div>
<div id="A1.p4" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A1.p4.1" class="ltx_p">The divergence is the operator <math id="A1.p4.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathrm{div}_{g}:\Gamma_{C^{\infty}}(TM)\rightarrow C^{\infty}(M)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>div</mi><mi>g</mi></msub><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Γ</mi><msup><mi>C</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">∞</mi></msup></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>T</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>M</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><mrow><msup><mi>C</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">∞</mi></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>M</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathrm{div}_{g}:\Gamma_{C^{\infty}}(TM)\rightarrow C^{\infty}(M)</annotation></semantics></math> making</p>
<table id="A1.E13" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A1.E13.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="d(\iota_{{}_{X}}\omega_{g})=\mathrm{div}_{g}X\cdot\omega_{g}\quad\mathrm{for~all}X\in\Gamma_{C^{\infty}}(TM)." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>d</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>ι</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>X</mi></msub></msub><msub><mi>ω</mi><mi>g</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>=</mo><msub><mi>div</mi><mi>g</mi></msub><mi>X</mi><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><msub><mi>ω</mi><mi>g</mi></msub><mi>for</mi><mi>all</mi><mi>X</mi><mo>∈</mo><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Γ</mi><msup><mi>C</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">∞</mi></msup></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>T</mi><mi>M</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">d(\iota_{{}_{X}}\omega_{g})=\mathrm{div}_{g}X\cdot\omega_{g}\quad\mathrm{for~all}X\in\Gamma_{C^{\infty}}(TM).</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(13)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A1.p4.2" class="ltx_p">where <math id="A1.p4.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\Gamma_{C^{\infty}}(TM)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Γ</mi><msup><mi>C</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">∞</mi></msup></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>T</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>M</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Gamma_{C^{\infty}}(TM)</annotation></semantics></math> represents the space of smooth sections of the tangent bundle.</p>
</div>
<div id="A1.p5" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A1.p5.1" class="ltx_p">The Laplacian on <math id="A1.p5.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(M,g)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>M</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>g</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(M,g)</annotation></semantics></math> is the operator defined as <math id="A1.p5.m2" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\Delta_{g}=-\mathrm{div}_{g}\circ\nabla_{g}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>g</mi></msub><mo rspace="0em">=</mo><mo lspace="0em">−</mo><mi>div</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>g</mi></msub><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">∘</mo><mo>∇</mo><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>g</mi></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Delta_{g}=-\mathrm{div}_{g}\circ\nabla_{g}</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>
</div>
<div id="A1.Thmtheorem1" class="ltx_theorem ltx_theorem_lemma">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_title_theorem"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_theorem"><span id="A1.Thmtheorem1.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Lemma A.1</span></span><span id="A1.Thmtheorem1.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">.</span></h6>
<div id="A1.Thmtheorem1.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A1.Thmtheorem1.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A1.Thmtheorem1.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">For any smooth functions <math id="A1.Thmtheorem1.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\varphi,\psi\in C^{\infty}(M)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>φ</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>ψ</mi></mrow><mo>∈</mo><mrow><msup><mi>C</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">∞</mi></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>M</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\varphi,\psi\in C^{\infty}(M)</annotation></semantics></math>, the Laplace-Beltrami operator <math id="A1.Thmtheorem1.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\Delta_{g}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mi>g</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Delta_{g}</annotation></semantics></math> satisfies the following product rule:</span></p>
</div>
<div id="A1.Thmtheorem1.p2" class="ltx_para">
<table id="A1.E14" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A1.E14.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\Delta_{g}(\varphi\cdot\psi)=\psi\Delta_{g}\varphi+\varphi\Delta_{g}\psi-2\left\langle\nabla_{g}\varphi,\nabla_{g}\psi\right\rangle_{g}." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mi>g</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>φ</mi><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><mi>ψ</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>ψ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mi>g</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>φ</mi></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mi>φ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mi>g</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>ψ</mi></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mrow><mo>⟨</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mo rspace="0.167em">∇</mo><mi>g</mi></msub><mi>φ</mi></mrow><mo>,</mo><mrow><msub><mo rspace="0.167em">∇</mo><mi>g</mi></msub><mi>ψ</mi></mrow></mrow><mo>⟩</mo></mrow><mi>g</mi></msub></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Delta_{g}(\varphi\cdot\psi)=\psi\Delta_{g}\varphi+\varphi\Delta_{g}\psi-2\left\langle\nabla_{g}\varphi,\nabla_{g}\psi\right\rangle_{g}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(14)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
<div id="A1.Thmtheorem1.p3" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A1.Thmtheorem1.p3.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A1.Thmtheorem1.p3.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">This identity generalizes the classical product rule of the Laplacian to Riemannian manifolds, where<math id="A1.Thmtheorem1.p3.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\langle\cdot,\cdot\rangle_{g}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">⟨</mo><mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">⋅</mo><mo rspace="0em">,</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">⋅</mo></mrow><mo stretchy="false">⟩</mo></mrow><mi>g</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\langle\cdot,\cdot\rangle_{g}</annotation></semantics></math> represents the Riemannian inner product with the metric <math id="A1.Thmtheorem1.p3.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="g" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>g</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">g</annotation></semantics></math>.</span></p>
</div>
</div>
<div id="A1.2" class="ltx_proof">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_font_italic ltx_title_proof">Proof.</h6>
<div id="A1.p6" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A1.p6.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A1.p6.1.1" class="ltx_text">To derive the formula for the divergence of a vector field on a Riemannian manifold, we begin by considering a smooth vector field</span></p>
<table id="A1.Ex1" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A1.Ex1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="X=\sum_{j=1}^{n}b_{j}\frac{\partial}{\partial x_{j}}\in\Gamma_{C^{\infty}}(TM)." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>X</mi><mo rspace="0.111em">=</mo><mrow><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>j</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>n</mi></munderover><mrow><msub><mi>b</mi><mi>j</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mfrac><mo>∂</mo><mrow><mo>∂</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>j</mi></msub></mrow></mfrac></mrow></mrow><mo>∈</mo><mrow><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Γ</mi><msup><mi>C</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">∞</mi></msup></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>T</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>M</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">X=\sum_{j=1}^{n}b_{j}\frac{\partial}{\partial x_{j}}\in\Gamma_{C^{\infty}}(TM).</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A1.p6.2" class="ltx_p"><span id="A1.p6.2.1" class="ltx_text">We express the contraction of <math id="A1.p6.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="X" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>X</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">X</annotation></semantics></math> with the volume form <math id="A1.p6.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\omega_{g}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>ω</mi><mi>g</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\omega_{g}</annotation></semantics></math>:</span></p>
</div>
<div id="A1.p7" class="ltx_para">
<table id="A1.E15" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_table">
<tbody>
<tr id="A1.E15X" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.E15X.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\iota_{{}_{X}}\omega_{g}\left(\frac{\partial}{\partial x_{1}},\ldots,\frac{\hat{\partial}}{\partial x_{i}},\ldots,\frac{\partial}{\partial x_{n}}\right)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>ι</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>X</mi></msub></msub><mi>ω</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>g</mi></msub><mo>(</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mo>∂</mo><mrow><mo>∂</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mn>1</mn></msub></mrow></mfrac></mstyle><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi><mo>,</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mover accent="true"><mo>∂</mo><mo>^</mo></mover><mrow><mo>∂</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></mrow></mfrac></mstyle><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi><mo>,</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mo>∂</mo><mrow><mo>∂</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>n</mi></msub></mrow></mfrac></mstyle><mo>)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\iota_{{}_{X}}\omega_{g}\left(\frac{\partial}{\partial x_{1}},\ldots,\frac{\hat{\partial}}{\partial x_{i}},\ldots,\frac{\partial}{\partial x_{n}}\right)</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.E15X.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=\omega_{g}\left(X,\frac{\partial}{\partial x_{1}},\ldots,\frac{\hat{\partial}}{\partial x_{i}},\ldots,\frac{\partial}{\partial x_{n}}\right)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><msub><mi>ω</mi><mi>g</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mi>X</mi><mo>,</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mo>∂</mo><mrow><mo>∂</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mn>1</mn></msub></mrow></mfrac></mstyle><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi><mo>,</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mover accent="true"><mo>∂</mo><mo>^</mo></mover><mrow><mo>∂</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></mrow></mfrac></mstyle><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi><mo>,</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mo>∂</mo><mrow><mo>∂</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>n</mi></msub></mrow></mfrac></mstyle><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=\omega_{g}\left(X,\frac{\partial}{\partial x_{1}},\ldots,\frac{\hat{\partial}}{\partial x_{i}},\ldots,\frac{\partial}{\partial x_{n}}\right)</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="4" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equationgroup ltx_align_right">(15)</span></td></tr>
<tr id="A1.E15Xa" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.E15Xa.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=(-1)^{i-1}\omega_{g}\left(\frac{\partial}{\partial x_{1}},\ldots,X,\ldots,\frac{\partial}{\partial x_{n}}\right)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>ω</mi><mi>g</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mo>∂</mo><mrow><mo>∂</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mn>1</mn></msub></mrow></mfrac></mstyle><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>X</mi><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi><mo>,</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mo>∂</mo><mrow><mo>∂</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>n</mi></msub></mrow></mfrac></mstyle><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=(-1)^{i-1}\omega_{g}\left(\frac{\partial}{\partial x_{1}},\ldots,X,\ldots,\frac{\partial}{\partial x_{n}}\right)</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr>
<tr id="A1.E15Xb" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.E15Xb.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=(-1)^{i-1}\sqrt{|\det g|}dx_{1}\wedge\cdots\wedge dx_{n}\left(\frac{\partial}{\partial x_{1}},\ldots,X,\ldots,\frac{\partial}{\partial x_{n}}\right)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msqrt><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><mrow><mo lspace="0em" movablelimits="false" rspace="0.167em">det</mo><mi>g</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow></msqrt><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>d</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mn>1</mn></msub></mrow><mo>∧</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">⋯</mo><mo>∧</mo><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>n</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mo>∂</mo><mrow><mo>∂</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mn>1</mn></msub></mrow></mfrac></mstyle><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>X</mi><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi><mo>,</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mo>∂</mo><mrow><mo>∂</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>n</mi></msub></mrow></mfrac></mstyle><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=(-1)^{i-1}\sqrt{|\det g|}dx_{1}\wedge\cdots\wedge dx_{n}\left(\frac{\partial}{\partial x_{1}},\ldots,X,\ldots,\frac{\partial}{\partial x_{n}}\right)</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr>
<tr id="A1.E15Xc" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.E15Xc.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=b_{i}(-1)^{i-1}\sqrt{|\det g|}." display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><msub><mi>b</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msqrt><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><mrow><mo lspace="0em" movablelimits="false" rspace="0.167em">det</mo><mi>g</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow></msqrt></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=b_{i}(-1)^{i-1}\sqrt{|\det g|}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
<div id="A1.p8" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A1.p8.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A1.p8.1.1" class="ltx_text">Next, we compute the exterior derivative of the contraction:</span></p>
</div>
<div id="A1.p9" class="ltx_para">
<table id="A1.E16" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_table">
<tbody>
<tr id="A1.E16X" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.E16X.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle d(\iota_{X}\omega_{g})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>ι</mi><mi>X</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>ω</mi><mi>g</mi></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle d(\iota_{X}\omega_{g})</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.E16X.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=d\left(\sum_{i=1}^{n}b_{i}(-1)^{i-1}\sqrt{|\det g|}dx_{1}\wedge\cdots\wedge\hat{dx_{i}}\wedge\cdots\wedge dx_{n}\right)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>n</mi></munderover></mstyle><mrow><msub><mi>b</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msqrt><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><mrow><mo lspace="0em" movablelimits="false" rspace="0.167em">det</mo><mi>g</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow></msqrt><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>d</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mn>1</mn></msub></mrow></mrow><mo>∧</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">⋯</mo><mo>∧</mo><mover accent="true"><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></mrow><mo>^</mo></mover><mo>∧</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">⋯</mo><mo>∧</mo><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>n</mi></msub></mrow></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=d\left(\sum_{i=1}^{n}b_{i}(-1)^{i-1}\sqrt{|\det g|}dx_{1}\wedge\cdots\wedge\hat{dx_{i}}\wedge\cdots\wedge dx_{n}\right)</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="4" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equationgroup ltx_align_right">(16)</span></td></tr>
<tr id="A1.E16Xa" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.E16Xa.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=\sum_{i=1}^{n}(-1)^{i-1}\frac{\partial}{\partial x_{i}}(b_{i}\sqrt{|\det g|})dx_{i}\wedge dx_{1}\wedge\cdots\wedge\hat{dx_{i}}\wedge\cdots\wedge dx_{n}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>n</mi></munderover></mstyle><mrow><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mo>∂</mo><mrow><mo>∂</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></mrow></mfrac></mstyle><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>b</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msqrt><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><mrow><mo lspace="0em" movablelimits="false" rspace="0.167em">det</mo><mi>g</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow></msqrt></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>d</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></mrow></mrow><mo>∧</mo><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mn>1</mn></msub></mrow><mo>∧</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">⋯</mo><mo>∧</mo><mover accent="true"><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></mrow><mo>^</mo></mover><mo>∧</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">⋯</mo><mo>∧</mo><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>n</mi></msub></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=\sum_{i=1}^{n}(-1)^{i-1}\frac{\partial}{\partial x_{i}}(b_{i}\sqrt{|\det g|})dx_{i}\wedge dx_{1}\wedge\cdots\wedge\hat{dx_{i}}\wedge\cdots\wedge dx_{n}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr>
<tr id="A1.E16Xb" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.E16Xb.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=\sum_{i=1}^{n}\frac{\partial}{\partial x_{i}}(b_{i}\sqrt{|\det g|})dx_{1}\wedge\cdots\wedge dx_{n}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>n</mi></munderover></mstyle><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mo>∂</mo><mrow><mo>∂</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></mrow></mfrac></mstyle><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>b</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msqrt><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><mrow><mo lspace="0em" movablelimits="false" rspace="0.167em">det</mo><mi>g</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow></msqrt></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>d</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mn>1</mn></msub></mrow></mrow><mo>∧</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">⋯</mo><mo>∧</mo><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>n</mi></msub></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=\sum_{i=1}^{n}\frac{\partial}{\partial x_{i}}(b_{i}\sqrt{|\det g|})dx_{1}\wedge\cdots\wedge dx_{n}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr>
<tr id="A1.E16Xc" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.E16Xc.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=\frac{1}{\sqrt{|\det g|}}\sum_{i=1}^{n}\frac{\partial}{\partial x_{i}}(b_{i}\sqrt{|\det g|})\cdot\omega_{g}." display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mn>1</mn><msqrt><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.167em">det</mo><mi>g</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow></msqrt></mfrac></mstyle><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>n</mi></munderover></mstyle><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mo>∂</mo><mrow><mo>∂</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></mrow></mfrac></mstyle><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>b</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msqrt><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><mrow><mo lspace="0em" movablelimits="false" rspace="0.167em">det</mo><mi>g</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow></msqrt></mrow><mo rspace="0.055em" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><msub><mi>ω</mi><mi>g</mi></msub></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=\frac{1}{\sqrt{|\det g|}}\sum_{i=1}^{n}\frac{\partial}{\partial x_{i}}(b_{i}\sqrt{|\det g|})\cdot\omega_{g}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
<div id="A1.p10" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A1.p10.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A1.p10.1.1" class="ltx_text">Since the divergence of a vector field is defined by <math id="A1.p10.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\operatorname{div}_{g}X=d(\iota_{X}\omega_{g})/\omega_{g}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>div</mi><mi>g</mi></msub><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><mi>X</mi></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>ι</mi><mi>X</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>ω</mi><mi>g</mi></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>/</mo><msub><mi>ω</mi><mi>g</mi></msub></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\operatorname{div}_{g}X=d(\iota_{X}\omega_{g})/\omega_{g}</annotation></semantics></math>, we obtain:</span></p>
</div>
<div id="A1.p11" class="ltx_para">
<table id="A1.E17" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A1.E17.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathrm{div}_{g}X=\frac{1}{\sqrt{|\det g|}}\sum_{i=1}^{n}\frac{\partial}{\partial x_{i}}(b_{i}\sqrt{|\det g|})." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>div</mi><mi>g</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>X</mi></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mfrac><mn>1</mn><msqrt><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.167em">det</mo><mi>g</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow></msqrt></mfrac><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>n</mi></munderover><mrow><mfrac><mo>∂</mo><mrow><mo>∂</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></mrow></mfrac><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>b</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msqrt><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><mrow><mo lspace="0em" movablelimits="false" rspace="0.167em">det</mo><mi>g</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow></msqrt></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathrm{div}_{g}X=\frac{1}{\sqrt{|\det g|}}\sum_{i=1}^{n}\frac{\partial}{\partial x_{i}}(b_{i}\sqrt{|\det g|}).</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(17)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
<div id="A1.p12" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A1.p12.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A1.p12.1.1" class="ltx_text">Now, we generalize this formula to the case where the vector field is multiplied by a smooth function <math id="A1.p12.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\varphi" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>φ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\varphi</annotation></semantics></math>:</span></p>
</div>
<div id="A1.p13" class="ltx_para">
<table id="A1.E18" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A1.E18.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\operatorname{div}_{g}(\varphi X)=\varphi\operatorname{div}_{g}X+\left\langle\nabla_{g}\varphi,X\right\rangle_{g}." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>div</mi><mi>g</mi></msub><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>φ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>X</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>φ</mi><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>div</mi><mi>g</mi></msub><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>X</mi></mrow><mo>+</mo><msub><mrow><mo>⟨</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mo rspace="0.167em">∇</mo><mi>g</mi></msub><mi>φ</mi></mrow><mo>,</mo><mi>X</mi></mrow><mo>⟩</mo></mrow><mi>g</mi></msub></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\operatorname{div}_{g}(\varphi X)=\varphi\operatorname{div}_{g}X+\left\langle\nabla_{g}\varphi,X\right\rangle_{g}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(18)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
<div id="A1.p14" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A1.p14.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A1.p14.1.1" class="ltx_text">This formula plays a crucial role in deriving the Laplace-Beltrami operator’s product rule. Using the definition <math id="A1.p14.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\Delta_{g}=-\operatorname{div}_{g}\nabla_{g}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mi>g</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo rspace="0.167em">−</mo><mrow><msub><mi>div</mi><mi>g</mi></msub><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><msub><mo>∇</mo><mi>g</mi></msub></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Delta_{g}=-\operatorname{div}_{g}\nabla_{g}</annotation></semantics></math>, we proceed to compute <math id="A1.p14.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\Delta_{g}(\varphi\psi)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mi>g</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>φ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>ψ</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Delta_{g}(\varphi\psi)</annotation></semantics></math>:</span></p>
</div>
<div id="A1.p15" class="ltx_para">
<table id="A1.E19" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_table">
<tbody>
<tr id="A1.E19X" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.E19X.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\Delta_{g}(\varphi\psi)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mi>g</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>φ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>ψ</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\Delta_{g}(\varphi\psi)</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.E19X.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=-{\rm div}_{g}\left(\nabla_{g}(\varphi\psi)\right)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><msub><mi>div</mi><mi>g</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><msub><mo>∇</mo><mi>g</mi></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>φ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>ψ</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=-{\rm div}_{g}\left(\nabla_{g}(\varphi\psi)\right)</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="6" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equationgroup ltx_align_right">(19)</span></td></tr>
<tr id="A1.E19Xa" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.E19Xa.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=-{\rm div}_{g}\left(\varphi\nabla_{g}\psi+\psi\nabla_{g}\varphi\right)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><msub><mi>div</mi><mi>g</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>φ</mi><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><msub><mo rspace="0.167em">∇</mo><mi>g</mi></msub><mi>ψ</mi></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mi>ψ</mi><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><msub><mo rspace="0.167em">∇</mo><mi>g</mi></msub><mi>φ</mi></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=-{\rm div}_{g}\left(\varphi\nabla_{g}\psi+\psi\nabla_{g}\varphi\right)</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr>
<tr id="A1.E19Xb" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.E19Xb.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=-\left[{\rm div}_{g}(\varphi\nabla_{g}\psi)+{\rm div}_{g}(\psi\nabla_{g}\varphi)\right]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mo>[</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>div</mi><mi>g</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>φ</mi><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><msub><mo rspace="0.167em">∇</mo><mi>g</mi></msub><mi>ψ</mi></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><msub><mi>div</mi><mi>g</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>ψ</mi><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><msub><mo rspace="0.167em">∇</mo><mi>g</mi></msub><mi>φ</mi></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>]</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=-\left[{\rm div}_{g}(\varphi\nabla_{g}\psi)+{\rm div}_{g}(\psi\nabla_{g}\varphi)\right]</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr>
<tr id="A1.E19Xc" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.E19Xc.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=-\Big[\varphi\,{\rm div}_{g}(\nabla_{g}\psi)+\langle\nabla_{g}\varphi,\nabla_{g}\psi\rangle_{g}+\psi\,{\rm div}_{g}(\nabla_{g}\varphi)+\langle\nabla_{g}\psi,\nabla_{g}\varphi\rangle_{g}\Big]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="1.600em" minsize="1.600em">[</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>φ</mi><mo lspace="0.170em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>div</mi><mi>g</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mo rspace="0.167em">∇</mo><mi>g</mi></msub><mi>ψ</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">⟨</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mo rspace="0.167em">∇</mo><mi>g</mi></msub><mi>φ</mi></mrow><mo>,</mo><mrow><msub><mo rspace="0.167em">∇</mo><mi>g</mi></msub><mi>ψ</mi></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">⟩</mo></mrow><mi>g</mi></msub><mo>+</mo><mrow><mi>ψ</mi><mo lspace="0.170em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>div</mi><mi>g</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mo rspace="0.167em">∇</mo><mi>g</mi></msub><mi>φ</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">⟨</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mo rspace="0.167em">∇</mo><mi>g</mi></msub><mi>ψ</mi></mrow><mo>,</mo><mrow><msub><mo rspace="0.167em">∇</mo><mi>g</mi></msub><mi>φ</mi></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">⟩</mo></mrow><mi>g</mi></msub></mrow><mo maxsize="1.600em" minsize="1.600em">]</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=-\Big[\varphi\,{\rm div}_{g}(\nabla_{g}\psi)+\langle\nabla_{g}\varphi,\nabla_{g}\psi\rangle_{g}+\psi\,{\rm div}_{g}(\nabla_{g}\varphi)+\langle\nabla_{g}\psi,\nabla_{g}\varphi\rangle_{g}\Big]</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr>
<tr id="A1.E19Xd" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.E19Xd.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=-\Big[\varphi\Delta_{g}\psi+\psi\Delta_{g}\varphi+2\langle\nabla_{g}\varphi,\nabla_{g}\psi\rangle_{g}\Big]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="1.600em" minsize="1.600em">[</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>φ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mi>g</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>ψ</mi></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mi>ψ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mi>g</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>φ</mi></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">⟨</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mo rspace="0.167em">∇</mo><mi>g</mi></msub><mi>φ</mi></mrow><mo>,</mo><mrow><msub><mo rspace="0.167em">∇</mo><mi>g</mi></msub><mi>ψ</mi></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">⟩</mo></mrow><mi>g</mi></msub></mrow></mrow><mo maxsize="1.600em" minsize="1.600em">]</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=-\Big[\varphi\Delta_{g}\psi+\psi\Delta_{g}\varphi+2\langle\nabla_{g}\varphi,\nabla_{g}\psi\rangle_{g}\Big]</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr>
<tr id="A1.E19Xe" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.E19Xe.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=\psi\Delta_{g}\varphi+\varphi\Delta_{g}\psi-2\langle\nabla_{g}\varphi,\nabla_{g}\psi\rangle_{g}." display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>ψ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mi>g</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>φ</mi></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mi>φ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mi>g</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>ψ</mi></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">⟨</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mo rspace="0.167em">∇</mo><mi>g</mi></msub><mi>φ</mi></mrow><mo>,</mo><mrow><msub><mo rspace="0.167em">∇</mo><mi>g</mi></msub><mi>ψ</mi></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">⟩</mo></mrow><mi>g</mi></msub></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=\psi\Delta_{g}\varphi+\varphi\Delta_{g}\psi-2\langle\nabla_{g}\varphi,\nabla_{g}\psi\rangle_{g}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
<div id="A1.p16" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A1.p16.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A1.p16.1.1" class="ltx_text">Thus, we have established the product rule for the Laplace-Beltrami operator on a Riemannian manifold.</span></p>
</div>
<div id="A1.p17" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A1.p17.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A1.p17.1.1" class="ltx_text">∎</span></p>
</div>
</div>
<div id="A1.p18" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A1.p18.1" class="ltx_p">Here we begin to proof the proposition 3.1:</p>
</div>
<div id="A1.3" class="ltx_proof">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_font_italic ltx_title_proof">Proof.</h6>
<div id="A1.p19" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A1.p19.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A1.p19.1.1" class="ltx_text">According to mathematical induction,</span></p>
</div>
<div id="A1.p20" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A1.p20.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A1.p20.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Base Case: L=1<span id="A1.p20.1.1.1" class="ltx_text"></span></span></p>
</div>
<div id="A1.p21" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A1.p21.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A1.p21.1.1" class="ltx_text">For <math id="A1.p21.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="L=1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>L</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">L=1</annotation></semantics></math>, the theorem reduces to the action of the Laplace-Beltrami operator on a single function <math id="A1.p21.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="g_{1}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>g</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">g_{1}</annotation></semantics></math>. By definition, if <math id="A1.p21.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="g_{1}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>g</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">g_{1}</annotation></semantics></math> is an eigenfunction of <math id="A1.p21.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\Delta_{\mathcal{M}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℳ</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Delta_{\mathcal{M}}</annotation></semantics></math> with eigenvalue <math id="A1.p21.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\lambda_{1}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>λ</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\lambda_{1}</annotation></semantics></math>, we have:</span></p>
</div>
<div id="A1.p22" class="ltx_para">
<table id="A1.E20" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A1.E20.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\Delta_{\mathcal{M}}g_{1}=\lambda_{1}g_{1}," display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℳ</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>g</mi><mn>1</mn></msub></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><msub><mi>λ</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>g</mi><mn>1</mn></msub></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Delta_{\mathcal{M}}g_{1}=\lambda_{1}g_{1},</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(20)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
<div id="A1.p23" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A1.p23.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A1.p23.1.1" class="ltx_text">which trivially satisfies the theorem. This establishes the base case.</span></p>
</div>
<div id="A1.p24" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A1.p24.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A1.p24.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Inductive Hypothesis: L=N<span id="A1.p24.1.1.1" class="ltx_text"></span></span></p>
</div>
<div id="A1.p25" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A1.p25.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A1.p25.1.1" class="ltx_text">Assume the theorem holds for <math id="A1.p25.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="L=N" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>L</mi><mo>=</mo><mi>N</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">L=N</annotation></semantics></math>, i,e.,for any product of <math id="A1.p25.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="N" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>N</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">N</annotation></semantics></math> eigenfunctions <math id="A1.p25.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="g_{1},g_{2},\ldots,g_{N}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>g</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>g</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>g</mi><mi>N</mi></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">g_{1},g_{2},\ldots,g_{N}</annotation></semantics></math> with corresponding eigenvalues <math id="A1.p25.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\lambda_{1},\lambda_{2},\ldots,\lambda_{N}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>λ</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>λ</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>λ</mi><mi>N</mi></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\lambda_{1},\lambda_{2},\ldots,\lambda_{N}</annotation></semantics></math>, the Laplace-Beltrami operator acts as:</span></p>
<table id="A1.E21" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A1.E21.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\Delta_{\mathcal{M}}\left(\prod_{i=1}^{N}g_{i}\right)=\left(\sum_{i=1}^{N}\lambda_{i}\right)\prod_{i=1}^{N}g_{i}." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℳ</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><munderover><mo lspace="0em" movablelimits="false">∏</mo><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>N</mi></munderover><msub><mi>g</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><munderover><mo lspace="0em" movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>N</mi></munderover><msub><mi>λ</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∏</mo><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>N</mi></munderover><msub><mi>g</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Delta_{\mathcal{M}}\left(\prod_{i=1}^{N}g_{i}\right)=\left(\sum_{i=1}^{N}\lambda_{i}\right)\prod_{i=1}^{N}g_{i}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(21)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
<div id="A1.p26" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A1.p26.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A1.p26.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Inductive Step: L=N+1<span id="A1.p26.1.1.1" class="ltx_text"></span></span></p>
</div>
<div id="A1.p27" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A1.p27.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A1.p27.1.1" class="ltx_text">We now prove the theorem for <math id="A1.p27.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="L=N+1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>L</mi><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>N</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">L=N+1</annotation></semantics></math>, we can get:</span></p>
<table id="A1.E22" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A1.E22.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\Delta_{\mathcal{M}}(\prod_{i=1}^{N+1}g_{i})=\Delta_{\mathcal{M}}\left[(\prod_{i=1}^{N}g_{i})g_{N+1}\right]." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℳ</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><munderover><mo lspace="0em" movablelimits="false">∏</mo><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mrow><mi>N</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></munderover><msub><mi>g</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℳ</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>[</mo><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><munderover><mo lspace="0em" movablelimits="false">∏</mo><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>N</mi></munderover><msub><mi>g</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>g</mi><mrow><mi>N</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub></mrow><mo>]</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Delta_{\mathcal{M}}(\prod_{i=1}^{N+1}g_{i})=\Delta_{\mathcal{M}}\left[(\prod_{i=1}^{N}g_{i})g_{N+1}\right].</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(22)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
<div id="A1.p28" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A1.p28.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A1.p28.1.1" class="ltx_text">Considering the Eq.  (<a href="#A1.E21" title="Equation 21 ‣ Proof. ‣ Appendix A Proof and Derivation ‣ Toward a Unified Geometry Understanding: Riemannian Diffusion Framework for Graph Generation and Prediction" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">21</span></a>) and Lemma <a href="#A1.Thmtheorem1" title="Lemma A.1. ‣ Appendix A Proof and Derivation ‣ Toward a Unified Geometry Understanding: Riemannian Diffusion Framework for Graph Generation and Prediction" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">A.1</span></a> , we can derive it as:</span></p>
</div>
<div id="A1.p29" class="ltx_para">
<table id="A1.E23" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_table">
<tbody>
<tr id="A1.E23X" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.E23X.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\Delta_{\mathcal{M}}(\prod_{i=1}^{N+1}g_{i})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℳ</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∏</mo><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mrow><mi>N</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></munderover></mstyle><msub><mi>g</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\Delta_{\mathcal{M}}(\prod_{i=1}^{N+1}g_{i})</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.E23X.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=\Delta_{\mathcal{M}}\left[\left(\prod_{i=1}^{N}g_{i}\right)g_{N+1}\right]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℳ</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>[</mo><mrow><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∏</mo><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>N</mi></munderover></mstyle><msub><mi>g</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>g</mi><mrow><mi>N</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub></mrow><mo>]</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=\Delta_{\mathcal{M}}\left[\left(\prod_{i=1}^{N}g_{i}\right)g_{N+1}\right]</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="5" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equationgroup ltx_align_right">(23)</span></td></tr>
<tr id="A1.E23Xa" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.E23Xa.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=g_{N+1}\Delta_{\mathcal{M}}\prod_{i=1}^{N}g_{i}+\prod_{i=1}^{N}g_{i}\Delta_{\mathcal{M}}g_{N+1}-2\left\langle\nabla_{\mathcal{M}}\prod_{i=1}^{N}g_{i},\nabla_{\mathcal{M}}g_{N+1}\right\rangle_{g}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo>=</mo><mi>g</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mrow><mi>N</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℳ</mi></msub><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mo movablelimits="false">∏</mo></mstyle><msub><mrow></mrow><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><msup><mrow></mrow><mi>N</mi></msup><mi>g</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>+</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mo movablelimits="false">∏</mo></mstyle><msub><mrow></mrow><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><msup><mrow></mrow><mi>N</mi></msup><mi>g</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>i</mi></msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℳ</mi></msub><mi>g</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mrow><mi>N</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><mo>−</mo><mn>2</mn><mo>⟨</mo><mo rspace="0.167em">∇</mo><msub><mrow></mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℳ</mi></msub><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mo movablelimits="false">∏</mo></mstyle><msub><mrow></mrow><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><msup><mrow></mrow><mi>N</mi></msup><mi>g</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><mo rspace="0.167em">∇</mo><msub><mrow></mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℳ</mi></msub><mi>g</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mrow><mi>N</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><mo>⟩</mo><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>g</mi></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=g_{N+1}\Delta_{\mathcal{M}}\prod_{i=1}^{N}g_{i}+\prod_{i=1}^{N}g_{i}\Delta_{\mathcal{M}}g_{N+1}-2\left\langle\nabla_{\mathcal{M}}\prod_{i=1}^{N}g_{i},\nabla_{\mathcal{M}}g_{N+1}\right\rangle_{g}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr>
<tr id="A1.E23Xb" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.E23Xb.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=g_{N+1}(\sum_{i=1}^{N}\lambda_{i})\prod_{i=1}^{N}g_{i}+(\prod_{i=1}^{N}g_{i})\lambda_{g_{N+1}}g_{N+1}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>g</mi><mrow><mi>N</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>N</mi></munderover></mstyle><msub><mi>λ</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∏</mo><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>N</mi></munderover></mstyle><msub><mi>g</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∏</mo><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>N</mi></munderover></mstyle><msub><mi>g</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>λ</mi><msub><mi>g</mi><mrow><mi>N</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>g</mi><mrow><mi>N</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=g_{N+1}(\sum_{i=1}^{N}\lambda_{i})\prod_{i=1}^{N}g_{i}+(\prod_{i=1}^{N}g_{i})\lambda_{g_{N+1}}g_{N+1}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr>
<tr id="A1.E23Xc" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.E23Xc.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=(\sum_{i=1}^{N}\lambda_{i})\prod_{i=1}^{N+1}g_{i}+\lambda_{N+1}\prod_{i=1}^{N+1}g_{i}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>N</mi></munderover></mstyle><msub><mi>λ</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∏</mo><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mrow><mi>N</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></munderover></mstyle><msub><mi>g</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><msub><mi>λ</mi><mrow><mi>N</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∏</mo><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mrow><mi>N</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></munderover></mstyle><msub><mi>g</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=(\sum_{i=1}^{N}\lambda_{i})\prod_{i=1}^{N+1}g_{i}+\lambda_{N+1}\prod_{i=1}^{N+1}g_{i}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr>
<tr id="A1.E23Xd" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.E23Xd.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=(\sum_{i=1}^{N+1}\lambda_{i})\prod_{i=1}^{N+1}g_{i}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mrow><mi>N</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></munderover></mstyle><msub><mi>λ</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∏</mo><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mrow><mi>N</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></munderover></mstyle><msub><mi>g</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=(\sum_{i=1}^{N+1}\lambda_{i})\prod_{i=1}^{N+1}g_{i}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
<div id="A1.p30" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A1.p30.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A1.p30.1.1" class="ltx_text">It can be observed that the theorem holds for <math id="A1.p30.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="L=N+1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>L</mi><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>N</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">L=N+1</annotation></semantics></math>. Thus, we have successfully proven the proposition 3.1.
∎</span></p>
</div>
</div>
</section>
<section id="A2" class="ltx_appendix">
<h2 class="ltx_title ltx_title_appendix"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_appendix">Appendix B </span>Preliminary</h2>

<section id="A2.SS1" class="ltx_subsection">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsection">B.1 </span>Preliminary of Riemannian Geometry</h3>

<div id="A2.SS1.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A2.SS1.p1.1" class="ltx_p">In this section, we provide a detailed introduction to Riemannian geometry.</p>
</div>
<div id="A2.SS1.p2" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A2.SS1.p2.1" class="ltx_p">A smooth manifold <math id="A2.SS1.p2.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="M" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>M</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">M</annotation></semantics></math> is termed a Riemannian manifold when equipped with a Riemannian metric <math id="A2.SS1.p2.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="g" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>g</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">g</annotation></semantics></math>. Curvature <math id="A2.SS1.p2.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="c" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>c</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">c</annotation></semantics></math> is a crucial measure that quantifies the extent of geodesic bending.
For each point <math id="A2.SS1.p2.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="x\in M" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo>∈</mo><mi>M</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">x\in M</annotation></semantics></math>, there exists a tangent space <math id="A2.SS1.p2.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="T_{x}M\subseteq\mathbb{R}^{d}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>T</mi><mi>x</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>M</mi></mrow><mo>⊆</mo><msup><mi>ℝ</mi><mi>d</mi></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">T_{x}M\subseteq\mathbb{R}^{d}</annotation></semantics></math> that surrounds <math id="A2.SS1.p2.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="x" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>x</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">x</annotation></semantics></math>, where the metric <math id="A2.SS1.p2.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="g" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>g</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">g</annotation></semantics></math> is applied to determine the manifold’s shape. The relationship between the tangent space and the manifold is established through exponential and logarithmic maps. Specifically, the exponential map at point <math id="A2.SS1.p2.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="x" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>x</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">x</annotation></semantics></math>, represented as <math id="A2.SS1.p2.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\exp_{x}^{c}(\cdot):T_{x}M\to M" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msubsup><mi>exp</mi><mi>x</mi><mi>c</mi></msubsup><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">⋅</mo><mo rspace="0.278em" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>T</mi><mi>x</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>M</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><mi>M</mi></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\exp_{x}^{c}(\cdot):T_{x}M\to M</annotation></semantics></math>, transforms points from the tangent space into the manifold, while the logarithmic map <math id="A2.SS1.p2.m10" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\log_{x}^{c}(\cdot)=(\exp_{x}^{c}(\cdot))^{-1}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msubsup><mi>log</mi><mi>x</mi><mi>c</mi></msubsup><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">⋅</mo><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>exp</mi><mi>x</mi><mi>c</mi></msubsup><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">⋅</mo><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\log_{x}^{c}(\cdot)=(\exp_{x}^{c}(\cdot))^{-1}</annotation></semantics></math> serves as its inverse..</p>
</div>
<div id="A2.SS1.p3" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A2.SS1.p3.1" class="ltx_p">In this paper, we use three geometric spaces of different curvature to form a product Riemannian manifold space: Euclidean space (<math id="A2.SS1.p3.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="c=0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>c</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">c=0</annotation></semantics></math>), hyperbolic space (<math id="A2.SS1.p3.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="c&lt;0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>c</mi><mo>&lt;</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">c&lt;0</annotation></semantics></math>), and spherical space (<math id="A2.SS1.p3.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="c&gt;0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>c</mi><mo>&gt;</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">c&gt;0</annotation></semantics></math>).</p>
</div>
<div id="A2.SS1.p4" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A2.SS1.p4.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A2.SS1.p4.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Hyperbolic space</span>.
A hyperbolic space is defined as <math id="A2.SS1.p4.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbb{H}_{c}^{d}{=\{\mathbf{x}_{p}\in\mathbb{R}^{d+1}:\langle\mathbf{x}_{p},\mathbf{x}_{p}\rangle_{\mathcal{L}}=1/c\}}," display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msubsup><mi>ℍ</mi><mi>c</mi><mi>d</mi></msubsup><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mrow><msub><mi>𝐱</mi><mi>p</mi></msub><mo>∈</mo><msup><mi>ℝ</mi><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup></mrow><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mrow><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">⟨</mo><mrow><msub><mi>𝐱</mi><mi>p</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>𝐱</mi><mi>p</mi></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">⟩</mo></mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℒ</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>/</mo><mi>c</mi></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbb{H}_{c}^{d}{=\{\mathbf{x}_{p}\in\mathbb{R}^{d+1}:\langle\mathbf{x}_{p},\mathbf{x}_{p}\rangle_{\mathcal{L}}=1/c\}},</annotation></semantics></math> where <math id="A2.SS1.p4.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="d" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>d</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">d</annotation></semantics></math> represents the dimension and the inner product is defined as <math id="A2.SS1.p4.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\langle\mathbf{x},\mathbf{y}\rangle_{\mathcal{L}}=-x_{1}y_{1}+\sum_{j=2}x_{j}y_{j}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">⟨</mo><mrow><mi>𝐱</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>𝐲</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">⟩</mo></mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℒ</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><msub><mi>x</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>y</mi><mn>1</mn></msub></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.055em">+</mo><mrow><msub><mo>∑</mo><mrow><mi>j</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></msub><mrow><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>j</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>y</mi><mi>j</mi></msub></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\langle\mathbf{x},\mathbf{y}\rangle_{\mathcal{L}}=-x_{1}y_{1}+\sum_{j=2}x_{j}y_{j}</annotation></semantics></math>). In a hyperbolic space, The geodesic distance between the two points is:</p>
</div>
<div id="A2.SS1.p5" class="ltx_para">
<table id="A2.E24" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A2.E24.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="d(x,y)=\frac{1}{\sqrt{-c}}\operatorname{arccosh}\left(c*\langle\mathbf{x},\mathbf{y}\rangle_{\mathcal{L}}\right)." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>y</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mfrac><mn>1</mn><msqrt><mrow><mo>−</mo><mi>c</mi></mrow></msqrt></mfrac><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mi>arccosh</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mi>c</mi><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">∗</mo><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">⟨</mo><mrow><mi>𝐱</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>𝐲</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">⟩</mo></mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℒ</mi></msub></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">d(x,y)=\frac{1}{\sqrt{-c}}\operatorname{arccosh}\left(c*\langle\mathbf{x},\mathbf{y}\rangle_{\mathcal{L}}\right).</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(24)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
<div id="A2.SS1.p6" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A2.SS1.p6.1" class="ltx_p">The exponential map in hyperbolic space is defined as:</p>
<table id="A2.E25" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A2.E25.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="exp_{x_{p}}^{c}(x)=\cosh\left(\sqrt{-c}||\mathbf{x}||\right)\mathbf{x}_{p}+\sinh\left(\sqrt{-c}||\mathbf{x}||\right)\frac{\mathbf{x}}{\sqrt{-c}||\mathbf{x}||}." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>e</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>x</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>p</mi><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>p</mi></msub><mi>c</mi></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>cosh</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><msqrt><mrow><mo>−</mo><mi>c</mi></mrow></msqrt><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mi>𝐱</mi><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>𝐱</mi><mi>p</mi></msub></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>sinh</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><msqrt><mrow><mo>−</mo><mi>c</mi></mrow></msqrt><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mi>𝐱</mi><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mfrac><mi>𝐱</mi><mrow><msqrt><mrow><mo>−</mo><mi>c</mi></mrow></msqrt><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mi>𝐱</mi><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow></mrow></mfrac></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">exp_{x_{p}}^{c}(x)=\cosh\left(\sqrt{-c}||\mathbf{x}||\right)\mathbf{x}_{p}+\sinh\left(\sqrt{-c}||\mathbf{x}||\right)\frac{\mathbf{x}}{\sqrt{-c}||\mathbf{x}||}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(25)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
<div id="A2.SS1.p7" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A2.SS1.p7.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A2.SS1.p7.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Sphere space</span>.
Sphere space is defined as <math id="A2.SS1.p7.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbb{S}_{c}^{d}=\{\mathbf{x}_{p}\in\mathbb{R}^{d+1}:\langle\mathbf{x}_{p},\mathbf{x}_{p}\rangle_{\mathbb{S}}=1/c\}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msubsup><mi>𝕊</mi><mi>c</mi><mi>d</mi></msubsup><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mrow><msub><mi>𝐱</mi><mi>p</mi></msub><mo>∈</mo><msup><mi>ℝ</mi><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup></mrow><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mrow><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">⟨</mo><mrow><msub><mi>𝐱</mi><mi>p</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>𝐱</mi><mi>p</mi></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">⟩</mo></mrow><mi>𝕊</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>/</mo><mi>c</mi></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbb{S}_{c}^{d}=\{\mathbf{x}_{p}\in\mathbb{R}^{d+1}:\langle\mathbf{x}_{p},\mathbf{x}_{p}\rangle_{\mathbb{S}}=1/c\}</annotation></semantics></math>, where the inner product is the standard Euclidean inner product
<math id="A2.SS1.p7.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\langle\mathbf{x},\mathbf{y}\rangle_{\mathbb{S}}=\sum_{j=1}^{d+1}x_{j}y_{j}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">⟨</mo><mrow><mi>𝐱</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>𝐲</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">⟩</mo></mrow><mi>𝕊</mi></msub><mo rspace="0.111em">=</mo><mrow><msubsup><mo>∑</mo><mrow><mi>j</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msubsup><mrow><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>j</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>y</mi><mi>j</mi></msub></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\langle\mathbf{x},\mathbf{y}\rangle_{\mathbb{S}}=\sum_{j=1}^{d+1}x_{j}y_{j}</annotation></semantics></math>.The geodesic distance between the two points is:</p>
</div>
<div id="A2.SS1.p8" class="ltx_para">
<table id="A2.E26" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A2.E26.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="d(x,y)=\frac{1}{\sqrt{c}}\arccos\left(c\langle\mathbf{x},\mathbf{y}\rangle_{\mathbb{S}}\right)." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>y</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mfrac><mn>1</mn><msqrt><mi>c</mi></msqrt></mfrac><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mi>arccos</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mi>c</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">⟨</mo><mrow><mi>𝐱</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>𝐲</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">⟩</mo></mrow><mi>𝕊</mi></msub></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">d(x,y)=\frac{1}{\sqrt{c}}\arccos\left(c\langle\mathbf{x},\mathbf{y}\rangle_{\mathbb{S}}\right).</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(26)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
<div id="A2.SS1.p9" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A2.SS1.p9.1" class="ltx_p">The exponential map in spherical space is defined as:</p>
</div>
<div id="A2.SS1.p10" class="ltx_para">
<table id="A2.E27" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A2.E27.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="exp_{x_{p}}^{c}(x)=\cosh\left(\sqrt{c}||\mathbf{x}||\right)\mathbf{x}_{p}+\sinh\left(\sqrt{c}||\mathbf{x}||\right)\frac{\mathbf{x}}{\sqrt{-c}||\mathbf{x}||}." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>e</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>x</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>p</mi><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>p</mi></msub><mi>c</mi></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>cosh</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><msqrt><mi>c</mi></msqrt><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mi>𝐱</mi><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>𝐱</mi><mi>p</mi></msub></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>sinh</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><msqrt><mi>c</mi></msqrt><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mi>𝐱</mi><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mfrac><mi>𝐱</mi><mrow><msqrt><mrow><mo>−</mo><mi>c</mi></mrow></msqrt><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mi>𝐱</mi><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow></mrow></mfrac></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">exp_{x_{p}}^{c}(x)=\cosh\left(\sqrt{c}||\mathbf{x}||\right)\mathbf{x}_{p}+\sinh\left(\sqrt{c}||\mathbf{x}||\right)\frac{\mathbf{x}}{\sqrt{-c}||\mathbf{x}||}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(27)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
<div id="A2.SS1.p11" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A2.SS1.p11.1" class="ltx_p">A product manifold is the Cartesian product <math id="A2.SS1.p11.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\mathcal{P}=\times_{i=1}^{n_{\mathcal{P}}}\mathcal{M}_{c_{i}}^{d_{i}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒫</mi><mo rspace="0em">=</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.222em">×</mo><msub><mrow></mrow><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><msup><mrow></mrow><msub><mi>n</mi><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒫</mi></msub></msup><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℳ</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><msub><mi>c</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></msub><msup><mrow></mrow><msub><mi>d</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{P}=\times_{i=1}^{n_{\mathcal{P}}}\mathcal{M}_{c_{i}}^{d_{i}}</annotation></semantics></math>, where <math id="A2.SS1.p11.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="c_{i}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>c</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">c_{i}</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="A2.SS1.p11.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="d_{i}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>d</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">d_{i}</annotation></semantics></math> are the curvature and dimensionality of the manifold <math id="A2.SS1.p11.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{M}_{K_{i}}^{c_{i}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msubsup><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℳ</mi><msub><mi>K</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><msub><mi>c</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></msubsup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{M}_{K_{i}}^{c_{i}}</annotation></semantics></math> respectively. If we restrict <math id="A2.SS1.p11.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{P}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒫</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{P}</annotation></semantics></math> to be composed of the Euclidean plane <math id="A2.SS1.p11.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbb{E}_{c_{\mathrm{E}}}^{d_{\mathrm{E}}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msubsup><mi>𝔼</mi><msub><mi>c</mi><mi>E</mi></msub><msub><mi>d</mi><mi>E</mi></msub></msubsup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbb{E}_{c_{\mathrm{E}}}^{d_{\mathrm{E}}}</annotation></semantics></math>, hyperboloids <math id="A2.SS1.p11.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbb{H}_{c_{j}^{\mathrm{H}}}^{d_{j}^{\mathrm{H}}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msubsup><mi>ℍ</mi><msubsup><mi>c</mi><mi>j</mi><mi>H</mi></msubsup><msubsup><mi>d</mi><mi>j</mi><mi>H</mi></msubsup></msubsup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbb{H}_{c_{j}^{\mathrm{H}}}^{d_{j}^{\mathrm{H}}}</annotation></semantics></math> and hyperspheres <math id="A2.SS1.p11.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbb{S}_{c_{j}^{\mathrm{S}}}^{d_{j}^{\mathrm{S}}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msubsup><mi>𝕊</mi><msubsup><mi>c</mi><mi>j</mi><mi>S</mi></msubsup><msubsup><mi>d</mi><mi>j</mi><mi>S</mi></msubsup></msubsup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbb{S}_{c_{j}^{\mathrm{S}}}^{d_{j}^{\mathrm{S}}}</annotation></semantics></math> of constant curvature, we can represent an arbitrary product manifold of model spaces as such:</p>
<table id="A2.E28" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A2.E28.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{P}=\mathbb{E}_{c_{\mathbb{E}}}^{d_{\mathbb{E}}}\times\left(\underset{j=1}{\operatorname*{\overset{n_{\mathbb{H}}}{\operatorname*{\operatorname*{\times}}}}}\mathbb{H}_{c_{j}^{\mathbb{H}}}^{d_{j}^{\mathbb{H}}}\right)\times\left(\underset{k=1}{\operatorname*{\overset{n_{\mathbb{S}}}{\operatorname*{\operatorname*{\times}}}}}\mathbb{S}_{c_{k}^{\mathbb{S}}}^{d_{k}^{\mathbb{S}}}\right)" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒫</mi><mo>=</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>𝔼</mi><msub><mi>c</mi><mi>𝔼</mi></msub><msub><mi>d</mi><mi>𝔼</mi></msub></msubsup><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">×</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><munderover accent="true" accentunder="true"><mo lspace="0em">×</mo><mrow><mi mathsize="0.700em">j</mi><mo mathsize="0.700em">=</mo><mn mathsize="0.700em">1</mn></mrow><msub><mi mathsize="0.700em">n</mi><mi mathsize="0.710em">ℍ</mi></msub></munderover><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>ℍ</mi><msubsup><mi>c</mi><mi>j</mi><mi>ℍ</mi></msubsup><msubsup><mi>d</mi><mi>j</mi><mi>ℍ</mi></msubsup></msubsup></mrow><mo rspace="0.055em">)</mo></mrow><mo rspace="0.222em">×</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><munderover accent="true" accentunder="true"><mo lspace="0em">×</mo><mrow><mi mathsize="0.700em">k</mi><mo mathsize="0.700em">=</mo><mn mathsize="0.700em">1</mn></mrow><msub><mi mathsize="0.700em">n</mi><mi mathsize="0.710em">𝕊</mi></msub></munderover><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>𝕊</mi><msubsup><mi>c</mi><mi>k</mi><mi>𝕊</mi></msubsup><msubsup><mi>d</mi><mi>k</mi><mi>𝕊</mi></msubsup></msubsup></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{P}=\mathbb{E}_{c_{\mathbb{E}}}^{d_{\mathbb{E}}}\times\left(\underset{j=1}{\operatorname*{\overset{n_{\mathbb{H}}}{\operatorname*{\operatorname*{\times}}}}}\mathbb{H}_{c_{j}^{\mathbb{H}}}^{d_{j}^{\mathbb{H}}}\right)\times\left(\underset{k=1}{\operatorname*{\overset{n_{\mathbb{S}}}{\operatorname*{\operatorname*{\times}}}}}\mathbb{S}_{c_{k}^{\mathbb{S}}}^{d_{k}^{\mathbb{S}}}\right)</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(28)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
<div id="A2.SS1.p12" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A2.SS1.p12.1" class="ltx_p">In Riemannian machine learning, each layer requires the conversion between exponential and logarithmic mappings. Although this process is conceptually natural, it is computationally complex and prone to instability. Notably, the equations associated with exponential mappings often lead to instability issues, such as values becoming excessively large or small, resulting in NaN (Not a Number) problems. Consequently, it is frequently necessary to meticulously identify appropriate hyperparameters to mitigate these issues.</p>
</div>
</section>
<section id="A2.SS2" class="ltx_subsection">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsection">B.2 </span>Kernel Method</h3>

<div id="A2.Thmtheorem1" class="ltx_theorem ltx_theorem_theorem">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_title_theorem"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_theorem"><span id="A2.Thmtheorem1.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Theorem B.1</span></span><span id="A2.Thmtheorem1.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">.</span></h6>
<div id="A2.Thmtheorem1.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A2.Thmtheorem1.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A2.Thmtheorem1.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">Bochner’s theorem <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_cite">[<a href="#bib.bib57" title="" class="ltx_ref">57</a>]</cite>: For any shift-invariant continuous kernel <math id="A2.Thmtheorem1.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="k(\boldsymbol{x},\boldsymbol{y})=k(\boldsymbol{x}-\boldsymbol{y})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝐱</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>𝐲</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>𝐱</mi><mo>−</mo><mi>𝐲</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">k(\boldsymbol{x},\boldsymbol{y})=k(\boldsymbol{x}-\boldsymbol{y})</annotation></semantics></math> defined on <math id="A2.Thmtheorem1.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbb{R}^{n}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mi>ℝ</mi><mi>n</mi></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbb{R}^{n}</annotation></semantics></math>,if <math id="A2.Thmtheorem1.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="p(\omega)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>ω</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">p(\omega)</annotation></semantics></math> is its Fourier transform and <math id="A2.Thmtheorem1.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="{\xi}_{\omega}(\boldsymbol{x})=\exp(i\langle\boldsymbol{\omega},\boldsymbol{x}\rangle)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>ξ</mi><mi>ω</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝐱</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>exp</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">⟨</mo><mrow><mi>𝛚</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>𝐱</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">⟩</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\xi}_{\omega}(\boldsymbol{x})=\exp(i\langle\boldsymbol{\omega},\boldsymbol{x}\rangle)</annotation></semantics></math>. then <math id="A2.Thmtheorem1.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="k" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>k</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">k</annotation></semantics></math> is positive definite if and only if <math id="A2.Thmtheorem1.p1.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="p\geq 0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo>≥</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">p\geq 0</annotation></semantics></math>. In this case if we sample <math id="A2.Thmtheorem1.p1.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\omega" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>ω</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\omega</annotation></semantics></math> according to the distribution proportional to <math id="A2.Thmtheorem1.p1.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="p(\omega)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>ω</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">p(\omega)</annotation></semantics></math>, the kernel <math id="A2.Thmtheorem1.p1.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="k" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>k</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">k</annotation></semantics></math> can be expressed as:</span></p>
</div>
<div id="A2.Thmtheorem1.p2" class="ltx_para">
<table id="A2.E29" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_table">
<tbody>
<tr id="A2.E29X" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A2.E29X.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle k(\boldsymbol{x}-\boldsymbol{y})=\int_{\mathbb{R}^{n}}p(\boldsymbol{\omega})\exp(i\langle\boldsymbol{\omega},\boldsymbol{x}-\boldsymbol{y}\rangle)d\boldsymbol{\omega}=k(\boldsymbol{0})\cdot\mathbb{E}_{\boldsymbol{\omega}\sim p}\left[\xi_{\boldsymbol{\omega}}(\boldsymbol{x})\xi_{\boldsymbol{\omega}}(\boldsymbol{y})^{*}\right]." display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>𝒙</mi><mo>−</mo><mi>𝒚</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><msub><mo>∫</mo><msup><mi>ℝ</mi><mi>n</mi></msup></msub></mstyle><mrow><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝝎</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mi>exp</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">⟨</mo><mrow><mi>𝝎</mi><mo>,</mo><mrow><mi>𝒙</mi><mo>−</mo><mi>𝒚</mi></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">⟩</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo rspace="0em">d</mo><mi>𝝎</mi></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>𝟎</mn><mo rspace="0.055em" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><msub><mi>𝔼</mi><mrow><mi>𝝎</mi><mo>∼</mo><mi>p</mi></mrow></msub></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>[</mo><mrow><msub><mi>ξ</mi><mi>𝝎</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝒙</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>ξ</mi><mi>𝝎</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝒚</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>∗</mo></msup></mrow><mo>]</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle k(\boldsymbol{x}-\boldsymbol{y})=\int_{\mathbb{R}^{n}}p(\boldsymbol{\omega})\exp(i\langle\boldsymbol{\omega},\boldsymbol{x}-\boldsymbol{y}\rangle)d\boldsymbol{\omega}=k(\boldsymbol{0})\cdot\mathbb{E}_{\boldsymbol{\omega}\sim p}\left[\xi_{\boldsymbol{\omega}}(\boldsymbol{x})\xi_{\boldsymbol{\omega}}(\boldsymbol{y})^{*}\right].</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equationgroup ltx_align_right">(29)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
</div>
<div id="A2.SS2.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A2.SS2.p1.1" class="ltx_p">Since both the probability distribution <math id="A2.SS2.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="p(\omega)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>ω</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">p(\omega)</annotation></semantics></math> and and the kernel <math id="A2.SS2.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="k" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>k</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">k</annotation></semantics></math> are real, the integral is unchanged when we replace the exponential with a cosine. Leveraging this property,  <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_cite">[<a href="#bib.bib29" title="" class="ltx_ref">29</a>]</cite> developed a hyperbolic Laplacian feature function within hyperbolic space <math id="A2.SS2.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbb{H}_{c}^{d}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msubsup><mi>ℍ</mi><mi>c</mi><mi>d</mi></msubsup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbb{H}_{c}^{d}</annotation></semantics></math>, yielding a hyperbolic Laplacian feature that approximates an invariance kernel in <math id="A2.SS2.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbb{H}_{c}^{d}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msubsup><mi>ℍ</mi><mi>c</mi><mi>d</mi></msubsup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbb{H}_{c}^{d}</annotation></semantics></math>:</p>
<table id="A2.E30" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A2.E30.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\operatorname{HyLa}_{\lambda,b,\boldsymbol{\omega}}(\boldsymbol{z})=\exp\left(\frac{n-1}{2}\langle\omega,\boldsymbol{z}\rangle_{H}\right)\cos\left(\lambda\langle\boldsymbol{\omega},\boldsymbol{z}\rangle_{H}+b\right)." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>HyLa</mi><mrow><mi>λ</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>b</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>𝝎</mi></mrow></msub><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝒛</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>exp</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mfrac><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mn>2</mn></mfrac><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">⟨</mo><mrow><mi>ω</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>𝒛</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">⟩</mo></mrow><mi>H</mi></msub></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mi>cos</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>λ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">⟨</mo><mrow><mi>𝝎</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>𝒛</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">⟩</mo></mrow><mi>H</mi></msub></mrow><mo>+</mo><mi>b</mi></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\operatorname{HyLa}_{\lambda,b,\boldsymbol{\omega}}(\boldsymbol{z})=\exp\left(\frac{n-1}{2}\langle\omega,\boldsymbol{z}\rangle_{H}\right)\cos\left(\lambda\langle\boldsymbol{\omega},\boldsymbol{z}\rangle_{H}+b\right).</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(30)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
<div id="A2.SS2.p2" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A2.SS2.p2.1" class="ltx_p"><cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_cite">[<a href="#bib.bib18" title="" class="ltx_ref">18</a>]</cite> generalized it to the more general Riemannian manifold. The Laplacian features of the Riemannian space are extracted by deriving the eigenfunction in the gyrovector ball <math id="A2.SS2.p2.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbb{G}_{\kappa}^{n}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msubsup><mi>𝔾</mi><mi>κ</mi><mi>n</mi></msubsup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbb{G}_{\kappa}^{n}</annotation></semantics></math>:</p>
</div>
<div id="A2.SS2.p3" class="ltx_para">
<table id="A2.E31" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A2.E31.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathrm{gF}_{\boldsymbol{\omega},b,\lambda}^{\kappa}(\boldsymbol{x})=A_{\boldsymbol{\omega},\boldsymbol{x}}\cos\left(\lambda\langle\boldsymbol{\omega},\boldsymbol{x}\rangle_{\kappa}+b\right),\boldsymbol{x}\in\mathbb{G}_{\kappa}^{n}," display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mrow><msubsup><mi>gF</mi><mrow><mi>𝝎</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>b</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>λ</mi></mrow><mi>κ</mi></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝒙</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><msub><mi>A</mi><mrow><mi>𝝎</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>𝒙</mi></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mi>cos</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>λ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">⟨</mo><mrow><mi>𝝎</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>𝒙</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">⟩</mo></mrow><mi>κ</mi></msub></mrow><mo>+</mo><mi>b</mi></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo><mrow><mi>𝒙</mi><mo>∈</mo><msubsup><mi>𝔾</mi><mi>κ</mi><mi>n</mi></msubsup></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathrm{gF}_{\boldsymbol{\omega},b,\lambda}^{\kappa}(\boldsymbol{x})=A_{\boldsymbol{\omega},\boldsymbol{x}}\cos\left(\lambda\langle\boldsymbol{\omega},\boldsymbol{x}\rangle_{\kappa}+b\right),\boldsymbol{x}\in\mathbb{G}_{\kappa}^{n},</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(31)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
<div id="A2.SS2.p4" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A2.SS2.p4.1" class="ltx_p">where <math id="A2.SS2.p4.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="A_{\boldsymbol{\omega},\boldsymbol{x}}=\exp\left(\frac{n-1}{2}\langle\omega,x\rangle_{\kappa}\right)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>A</mi><mrow><mi>𝝎</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>𝒙</mi></mrow></msub><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>exp</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mfrac><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mn>2</mn></mfrac><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">⟨</mo><mrow><mi>ω</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>x</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">⟩</mo></mrow><mi>κ</mi></msub></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">A_{\boldsymbol{\omega},\boldsymbol{x}}=\exp\left(\frac{n-1}{2}\langle\omega,x\rangle_{\kappa}\right)</annotation></semantics></math>, <math id="A2.SS2.p4.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\langle\omega,x\rangle_{\kappa}=\log\frac{1+\kappa\|\boldsymbol{x}\|^{2}}{\|\boldsymbol{x}-\boldsymbol{\omega}\|^{2}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">⟨</mo><mrow><mi>ω</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>x</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">⟩</mo></mrow><mi>κ</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><mfrac><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>+</mo><mrow><mi>κ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mi>𝒙</mi><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow></mrow><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mrow><mi>𝒙</mi><mo>−</mo><mi>𝝎</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup></mfrac></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\langle\omega,x\rangle_{\kappa}=\log\frac{1+\kappa\|\boldsymbol{x}\|^{2}}{\|\boldsymbol{x}-\boldsymbol{\omega}\|^{2}}</annotation></semantics></math></p>
</div>
<div id="A2.SS2.p5" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A2.SS2.p5.1" class="ltx_p">Using the Eq. (<a href="#A2.E31" title="Equation 31 ‣ B.2 Kernel Method ‣ Appendix B Preliminary ‣ Toward a Unified Geometry Understanding: Riemannian Diffusion Framework for Graph Generation and Prediction" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">31</span></a>), a generalized Fourier map <math id="A2.SS2.p5.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\phi_{\mathrm{gF}}(\boldsymbol{x})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>ϕ</mi><mi>gF</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝒙</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\phi_{\mathrm{gF}}(\boldsymbol{x})</annotation></semantics></math> can be constructed to estimate an equidistant-invariant kernel on a Riemannian space. Moreover, this kernel can be seen as a generalization of Poisson’s kernel in hyperbolic space.</p>
</div>
<div id="A2.SS2.p6" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A2.SS2.p6.1" class="ltx_p">This kernel method can be applied to two types of features: node embeddings and feature embeddings. For node embeddings, a Riemannian feature representation must first be constructed for each individual node <math id="A2.SS2.p6.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="z_{i}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>z</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">z_{i}</annotation></semantics></math>. Then, the inner product <math id="A2.SS2.p6.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\langle\phi_{\mathrm{gF}}(\boldsymbol{z}{i}),\phi{\mathrm{gF}}(\boldsymbol{z}_{j})\rangle" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">⟨</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>ϕ</mi><mi>gF</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>𝒛</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>i</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo><mrow><mi>ϕ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>gF</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>𝒛</mi><mi>j</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">⟩</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\langle\phi_{\mathrm{gF}}(\boldsymbol{z}{i}),\phi{\mathrm{gF}}(\boldsymbol{z}_{j})\rangle</annotation></semantics></math> between nodes <math id="A2.SS2.p6.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="v_{i}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>v</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">v_{i}</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="A2.SS2.p6.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="v_{j}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>v</mi><mi>j</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">v_{j}</annotation></semantics></math> approximates a kernel function <math id="A2.SS2.p6.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="k(z_{i},z_{j})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>z</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>z</mi><mi>j</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">k(z_{i},z_{j})</annotation></semantics></math>. The optimization of <math id="A2.SS2.p6.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\boldsymbol{z}_{i}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>𝒛</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\boldsymbol{z}_{i}</annotation></semantics></math> is driven by the goal of learning an effective kernel over the product space to support downstream tasks.
For feature embeddings, we represent normalized node feature as <math id="A2.SS2.p6.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbf{X}\in\mathbb{R}^{n\times d}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>𝐗</mi><mo>∈</mo><msup><mi>ℝ</mi><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">×</mo><mi>d</mi></mrow></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbf{X}\in\mathbb{R}^{n\times d}</annotation></semantics></math> and inital Riemannian embedding
as <math id="A2.SS2.p6.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="z_{i}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>z</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">z_{i}</annotation></semantics></math>. Then it can be calculated by <math id="A2.SS2.p6.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\sum_{k=1}^{d}\mathbf{X}_{ik}\phi_{\mathrm{gF}}(\boldsymbol{z}_{k})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msubsup><mo>∑</mo><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>d</mi></msubsup><mrow><msub><mi>𝐗</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>k</mi></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>ϕ</mi><mi>gF</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>𝒛</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\sum_{k=1}^{d}\mathbf{X}_{ik}\phi_{\mathrm{gF}}(\boldsymbol{z}_{k})</annotation></semantics></math>. Its inner product between two features is:</p>
</div>
<div id="A2.SS2.p7" class="ltx_para">
<table id="A2.E32" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A2.E32.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\langle\sum_{k=1}^{d}\mathbf{X}_{ik}\phi_{\mathrm{gF}}(\boldsymbol{z}_{k}),\sum_{l=1}^{d}\mathbf{X}_{jl}\phi_{\mathrm{gF}}(\boldsymbol{z}_{l})\rangle=\sum_{k,l=1}^{d}\mathbf{X}_{ik}\mathbf{X}_{jl}\langle\phi_{\mathrm{gF}}(\boldsymbol{z}_{k}),\phi_{\mathrm{gF}}(\boldsymbol{z}_{l})\rangle." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">⟨</mo><mrow><mrow><munderover><mo lspace="0em" movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>d</mi></munderover><mrow><msub><mi>𝐗</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>k</mi></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>ϕ</mi><mi>gF</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>𝒛</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0em">,</mo><mrow><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>l</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>d</mi></munderover><mrow><msub><mi>𝐗</mi><mrow><mi>j</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>l</mi></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>ϕ</mi><mi>gF</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>𝒛</mi><mi>l</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">⟩</mo></mrow><mo rspace="0.111em">=</mo><mrow><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>l</mi></mrow><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>d</mi></munderover><mrow><msub><mi>𝐗</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>k</mi></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>𝐗</mi><mrow><mi>j</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>l</mi></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">⟨</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>ϕ</mi><mi>gF</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>𝒛</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo><mrow><msub><mi>ϕ</mi><mi>gF</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>𝒛</mi><mi>l</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">⟩</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\langle\sum_{k=1}^{d}\mathbf{X}_{ik}\phi_{\mathrm{gF}}(\boldsymbol{z}_{k}),\sum_{l=1}^{d}\mathbf{X}_{jl}\phi_{\mathrm{gF}}(\boldsymbol{z}_{l})\rangle=\sum_{k,l=1}^{d}\mathbf{X}_{ik}\mathbf{X}_{jl}\langle\phi_{\mathrm{gF}}(\boldsymbol{z}_{k}),\phi_{\mathrm{gF}}(\boldsymbol{z}_{l})\rangle.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(32)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
</section>
<section id="A2.SS3" class="ltx_subsection">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsection">B.3 </span>Preliminary of Diffusion Model</h3>

<div id="A2.SS3.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A2.SS3.p1.1" class="ltx_p">Denoising Diffusion Probabilistic Models (DDPMs) <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_cite">[<a href="#bib.bib13" title="" class="ltx_ref">13</a>]</cite> are a class of generative models based on diffusion processes that generate high-quality samples by simulating a step-by-step denoising process, transforming noise into realistic data. The core idea of DDPMs is to construct a generative model through two complementary processes: a forward process that gradually adds noise to data, and a reverse process that learns to iteratively denoise and reconstruct the data distribution.</p>
</div>
<div id="A2.SS3.p2" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A2.SS3.p2.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A2.SS3.p2.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Forward Process</span>: the forward process <math id="A2.SS3.p2.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="q(z|x)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>q</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>z</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">|</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">q(z|x)</annotation></semantics></math> is the variance-preserving Markov process:</p>
</div>
<div id="A2.SS3.p3" class="ltx_para">
<table id="A2.E33" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A2.E33.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="q(\mathbf{z}_{\lambda}|\mathbf{x})=\mathcal{N}(\alpha_{\lambda}\mathbf{x},\sigma_{\lambda}^{2}\mathbf{I}),\mathrm{where}\alpha_{\lambda}^{2}=1/(1+e^{-\lambda}),\sigma_{\lambda}^{2}=1-\alpha_{\lambda}^{2}" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>q</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>𝐳</mi><mi>λ</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">|</mo><mi>𝐱</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒩</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>α</mi><mi>λ</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>𝐱</mi></mrow><mo>,</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>σ</mi><mi>λ</mi><mn>2</mn></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>𝐈</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>where</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>α</mi><mi>λ</mi><mn>2</mn></msubsup></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>/</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>+</mo><msup><mi>e</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mi>λ</mi></mrow></msup></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>σ</mi><mi>λ</mi><mn>2</mn></msubsup><mo>=</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><msubsup><mi>α</mi><mi>λ</mi><mn>2</mn></msubsup></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">q(\mathbf{z}_{\lambda}|\mathbf{x})=\mathcal{N}(\alpha_{\lambda}\mathbf{x},\sigma_{\lambda}^{2}\mathbf{I}),\mathrm{where}\alpha_{\lambda}^{2}=1/(1+e^{-\lambda}),\sigma_{\lambda}^{2}=1-\alpha_{\lambda}^{2}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(33)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A2.SS3.p3.1" class="ltx_p">For intermediate steps, the transition between noise levels is given by:</p>
<table id="A2.E34" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A2.E34.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="q(\mathbf{z}_{\lambda}|\mathbf{z}_{\lambda^{\prime}})=\mathcal{N}((\alpha_{\lambda}/\alpha_{\lambda^{\prime}})\mathbf{z}_{\lambda^{\prime}},\sigma_{\lambda|\lambda^{\prime}}^{2}\mathbf{I}),\mathrm{where}\lambda&lt;\lambda^{\prime},\sigma_{\lambda|\lambda^{\prime}}^{2}=(1-e^{\lambda-\lambda^{\prime}})\sigma_{\lambda}^{2}" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>q</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>𝐳</mi><mi>λ</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">|</mo><msub><mi>𝐳</mi><msup><mi>λ</mi><mo>′</mo></msup></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒩</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>α</mi><mi>λ</mi></msub><mo>/</mo><msub><mi>α</mi><msup><mi>λ</mi><mo>′</mo></msup></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>𝐳</mi><msup><mi>λ</mi><mo>′</mo></msup></msub></mrow><mo>,</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>σ</mi><mrow><mi>λ</mi><mo fence="false">|</mo><msup><mi>λ</mi><mo>′</mo></msup></mrow><mn>2</mn></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>𝐈</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>where</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>λ</mi></mrow><mo>&lt;</mo><msup><mi>λ</mi><mo>′</mo></msup></mrow><mo>,</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>σ</mi><mrow><mi>λ</mi><mo fence="false">|</mo><msup><mi>λ</mi><mo>′</mo></msup></mrow><mn>2</mn></msubsup><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><msup><mi>e</mi><mrow><mi>λ</mi><mo>−</mo><msup><mi>λ</mi><mo>′</mo></msup></mrow></msup></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>σ</mi><mi>λ</mi><mn>2</mn></msubsup></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">q(\mathbf{z}_{\lambda}|\mathbf{z}_{\lambda^{\prime}})=\mathcal{N}((\alpha_{\lambda}/\alpha_{\lambda^{\prime}})\mathbf{z}_{\lambda^{\prime}},\sigma_{\lambda|\lambda^{\prime}}^{2}\mathbf{I}),\mathrm{where}\lambda&lt;\lambda^{\prime},\sigma_{\lambda|\lambda^{\prime}}^{2}=(1-e^{\lambda-\lambda^{\prime}})\sigma_{\lambda}^{2}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(34)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
<div id="A2.SS3.p4" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A2.SS3.p4.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A2.SS3.p4.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Reverse Process</span>:
The reverse process is a generative model that starts from a prior distribution <math id="A2.SS3.p4.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="p_{\theta}(\mathbf{z}_{\lambda_{\mathrm{min}}})=\mathcal{N}(\mathbf{0},\mathbf{I})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>p</mi><mi>θ</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>𝐳</mi><msub><mi>λ</mi><mi>min</mi></msub></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒩</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>𝟎</mn><mo>,</mo><mi>𝐈</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">p_{\theta}(\mathbf{z}_{\lambda_{\mathrm{min}}})=\mathcal{N}(\mathbf{0},\mathbf{I})</annotation></semantics></math> and reconstructs the real data distribution by iteratively denoising the data. The reverse transition is modeled as:</p>
</div>
<div id="A2.SS3.p5" class="ltx_para">
<table id="A2.E35" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A2.E35.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="p_{\theta}(\mathbf{z}_{\lambda^{\prime}}|\mathbf{z}_{\lambda})=\mathcal{N}(\tilde{\boldsymbol{\mu}}_{\lambda^{\prime}|\lambda}(\mathbf{z}_{\lambda},\mathbf{x}_{\theta}(\mathbf{z}_{\lambda})),(\tilde{\sigma}_{\lambda^{\prime}|\lambda}^{2})^{1-v}(\sigma_{\lambda|\lambda^{\prime}}^{2})^{v})" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>p</mi><mi>θ</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>𝐳</mi><msup><mi>λ</mi><mo>′</mo></msup></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">|</mo><msub><mi>𝐳</mi><mi>λ</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒩</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>𝝁</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mrow><msup><mi>λ</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo fence="false">|</mo><mi>λ</mi></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>𝐳</mi><mi>λ</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><mrow><msub><mi>𝐱</mi><mi>θ</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>𝐳</mi><mi>λ</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo><mrow><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msubsup><mover accent="true"><mi>σ</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mrow><msup><mi>λ</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo fence="false">|</mo><mi>λ</mi></mrow><mn>2</mn></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mi>v</mi></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msubsup><mi>σ</mi><mrow><mi>λ</mi><mo fence="false">|</mo><msup><mi>λ</mi><mo>′</mo></msup></mrow><mn>2</mn></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mi>v</mi></msup></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">p_{\theta}(\mathbf{z}_{\lambda^{\prime}}|\mathbf{z}_{\lambda})=\mathcal{N}(\tilde{\boldsymbol{\mu}}_{\lambda^{\prime}|\lambda}(\mathbf{z}_{\lambda},\mathbf{x}_{\theta}(\mathbf{z}_{\lambda})),(\tilde{\sigma}_{\lambda^{\prime}|\lambda}^{2})^{1-v}(\sigma_{\lambda|\lambda^{\prime}}^{2})^{v})</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(35)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
<div id="A2.SS3.p6" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A2.SS3.p6.1" class="ltx_p">where <math id="A2.SS3.p6.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\tilde{\boldsymbol{\mu}}_{\lambda^{\prime}|\lambda}(\mathbf{z}_{\lambda},\mathbf{x})=e^{\lambda-\lambda^{\prime}}(\alpha_{\lambda^{\prime}}/\alpha_{\lambda})\mathbf{z}_{\lambda}+(1-e^{\lambda-\lambda^{\prime}})\alpha_{\lambda^{\prime}}\mathbf{x}," display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>𝝁</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mrow><msup><mi>λ</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo fence="false">|</mo><mi>λ</mi></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>𝐳</mi><mi>λ</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><mi>𝐱</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><msup><mi>e</mi><mrow><mi>λ</mi><mo>−</mo><msup><mi>λ</mi><mo>′</mo></msup></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>α</mi><msup><mi>λ</mi><mo>′</mo></msup></msub><mo>/</mo><msub><mi>α</mi><mi>λ</mi></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>𝐳</mi><mi>λ</mi></msub></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><msup><mi>e</mi><mrow><mi>λ</mi><mo>−</mo><msup><mi>λ</mi><mo>′</mo></msup></mrow></msup></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>α</mi><msup><mi>λ</mi><mo>′</mo></msup></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>𝐱</mi></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\tilde{\boldsymbol{\mu}}_{\lambda^{\prime}|\lambda}(\mathbf{z}_{\lambda},\mathbf{x})=e^{\lambda-\lambda^{\prime}}(\alpha_{\lambda^{\prime}}/\alpha_{\lambda})\mathbf{z}_{\lambda}+(1-e^{\lambda-\lambda^{\prime}})\alpha_{\lambda^{\prime}}\mathbf{x},</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="A2.SS3.p6.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\tilde{\sigma}_{\lambda^{\prime}|\lambda}^{2}=(1-e^{\lambda-\lambda^{\prime}})\sigma_{\lambda^{\prime}}^{2}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msubsup><mover accent="true"><mi>σ</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mrow><msup><mi>λ</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo fence="false">|</mo><mi>λ</mi></mrow><mn>2</mn></msubsup><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><msup><mi>e</mi><mrow><mi>λ</mi><mo>−</mo><msup><mi>λ</mi><mo>′</mo></msup></mrow></msup></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>σ</mi><msup><mi>λ</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mn>2</mn></msubsup></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\tilde{\sigma}_{\lambda^{\prime}|\lambda}^{2}=(1-e^{\lambda-\lambda^{\prime}})\sigma_{\lambda^{\prime}}^{2}</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>
</div>
<div id="A2.SS3.p7" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A2.SS3.p7.1" class="ltx_p">The model is trained to predict the noise at each step by minimizing the objective function, which measures the discrepancy between the predicted noise and the actual noise added during the forward process. Specifically, the training objective is formulated as:
<math id="A2.SS3.p7.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbb{E}_{\boldsymbol{\epsilon},\lambda}\left[\|\boldsymbol{\epsilon}_{\theta}(\mathbf{z}_{\lambda})-\boldsymbol{\epsilon}\|_{2}^{2}\right]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>𝔼</mi><mrow><mi class="ltx_mathvariant_bold-italic" mathvariant="bold-italic">ϵ</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>λ</mi></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>[</mo><msubsup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mi class="ltx_mathvariant_bold-italic" mathvariant="bold-italic">ϵ</mi><mi>θ</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>𝐳</mi><mi>λ</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mi class="ltx_mathvariant_bold-italic" mathvariant="bold-italic">ϵ</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn><mn>2</mn></msubsup><mo>]</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbb{E}_{\boldsymbol{\epsilon},\lambda}\left[\|\boldsymbol{\epsilon}_{\theta}(\mathbf{z}_{\lambda})-\boldsymbol{\epsilon}\|_{2}^{2}\right]</annotation></semantics></math></p>
</div>
<div id="A2.SS3.p8" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A2.SS3.p8.1" class="ltx_p">To enhance the controllability and quality of generated samples, DDPMs often employ guidance mechanisms:</p>
</div>
<div id="A2.SS3.p9" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A2.SS3.p9.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A2.SS3.p9.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Classifier Guidance</span>: Classifier guidance <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_cite">[<a href="#bib.bib58" title="" class="ltx_ref">58</a>]</cite> introduces a conditional diffusion process by leveraging a pre-trained classifier <math id="A2.SS3.p9.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="p_{\theta}(\mathbf{c}|\mathbf{z}_{\lambda})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>p</mi><mi>θ</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝐜</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">|</mo><msub><mi>𝐳</mi><mi>λ</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">p_{\theta}(\mathbf{c}|\mathbf{z}_{\lambda})</annotation></semantics></math>. The guided noise prediction is given by:</p>
</div>
<div id="A2.SS3.p10" class="ltx_para">
<table id="A2.E36" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A2.E36.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\tilde{\epsilon}_{\theta}(\mathbf{z}_{\lambda},\mathbf{c})=\epsilon_{\theta}(\mathbf{z}_{\lambda},\mathbf{c})-w\sigma_{\lambda}\nabla_{\mathbf{z}_{\lambda}}\log p_{\theta}(\mathbf{c}|\mathbf{z}_{\lambda})\approx-\sigma_{\lambda}\nabla_{\mathbf{z}_{\lambda}}[\log p(\mathbf{z}_{\lambda}|\mathbf{c})+w\log p_{\theta}(\mathbf{c}|\mathbf{z}_{\lambda})]," display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>ϵ</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mi>θ</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>𝐳</mi><mi>λ</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><mi>𝐜</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>ϵ</mi><mi>θ</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>𝐳</mi><mi>λ</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><mi>𝐜</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi>w</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>σ</mi><mi>λ</mi></msub><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mo>∇</mo><msub><mi>𝐳</mi><mi>λ</mi></msub></msub><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>log</mi><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>p</mi><mi>θ</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝐜</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">|</mo><msub><mi>𝐳</mi><mi>λ</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>≈</mo><mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><msub><mi>σ</mi><mi>λ</mi></msub><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><msub><mo>∇</mo><msub><mi>𝐳</mi><mi>λ</mi></msub></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>𝐳</mi><mi>λ</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">|</mo><mi>𝐜</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mi>w</mi><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>log</mi><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>p</mi><mi>θ</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝐜</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">|</mo><msub><mi>𝐳</mi><mi>λ</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\tilde{\epsilon}_{\theta}(\mathbf{z}_{\lambda},\mathbf{c})=\epsilon_{\theta}(\mathbf{z}_{\lambda},\mathbf{c})-w\sigma_{\lambda}\nabla_{\mathbf{z}_{\lambda}}\log p_{\theta}(\mathbf{c}|\mathbf{z}_{\lambda})\approx-\sigma_{\lambda}\nabla_{\mathbf{z}_{\lambda}}[\log p(\mathbf{z}_{\lambda}|\mathbf{c})+w\log p_{\theta}(\mathbf{c}|\mathbf{z}_{\lambda})],</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(36)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
<div id="A2.SS3.p11" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A2.SS3.p11.1" class="ltx_p">where <math id="A2.SS3.p11.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="w" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>w</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">w</annotation></semantics></math> controls the strength of the guidance. This can be interpreted as:</p>
</div>
<div id="A2.SS3.p12" class="ltx_para">
<table id="A2.E37" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A2.E37.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\left.\tilde{\epsilon}_{\theta}(\mathbf{z}_{\lambda},\mathbf{c})\approx-\sigma_{\lambda}\nabla_{\mathbf{z}_{\lambda}}\left[\log p(\mathbf{z}_{\lambda}|\mathbf{c})\right.+w\log p_{\theta}(\mathbf{c}|\mathbf{z}_{\lambda})\right]." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>ϵ</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mi>θ</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>𝐳</mi><mi>λ</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><mi>𝐜</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>≈</mo><mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><msub><mi>σ</mi><mi>λ</mi></msub><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><msub><mo>∇</mo><msub><mi>𝐳</mi><mi>λ</mi></msub></msub><mrow><mo>[</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>𝐳</mi><mi>λ</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">|</mo><mi>𝐜</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mi>w</mi><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><msub><mi>p</mi><mi>θ</mi></msub></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝐜</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">|</mo><msub><mi>𝐳</mi><mi>λ</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>]</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\left.\tilde{\epsilon}_{\theta}(\mathbf{z}_{\lambda},\mathbf{c})\approx-\sigma_{\lambda}\nabla_{\mathbf{z}_{\lambda}}\left[\log p(\mathbf{z}_{\lambda}|\mathbf{c})\right.+w\log p_{\theta}(\mathbf{c}|\mathbf{z}_{\lambda})\right].</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(37)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
<div id="A2.SS3.p13" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A2.SS3.p13.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A2.SS3.p13.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Classifier-free Guidance</span>:
Classifier-free guidance <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_cite">[<a href="#bib.bib59" title="" class="ltx_ref">59</a>]</cite> eliminates the need for a separate classifier by jointly training conditional and unconditional models. The guided noise prediction is computed as:</p>
</div>
<div id="A2.SS3.p14" class="ltx_para">
<table id="A2.E38" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A2.E38.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\tilde{\boldsymbol{\epsilon}}_{\theta}(\mathbf{z}_{\lambda},\mathbf{c})=(1+w)\boldsymbol{\epsilon}_{\theta}(\mathbf{z}_{\lambda},\mathbf{c})-w\boldsymbol{\epsilon}_{\theta}(\mathbf{z}_{\lambda})" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mover accent="true"><mi class="ltx_mathvariant_bold-italic" mathvariant="bold-italic">ϵ</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mi>θ</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>𝐳</mi><mi>λ</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><mi>𝐜</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>+</mo><mi>w</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_mathvariant_bold-italic" mathvariant="bold-italic">ϵ</mi><mi>θ</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>𝐳</mi><mi>λ</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><mi>𝐜</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi>w</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_mathvariant_bold-italic" mathvariant="bold-italic">ϵ</mi><mi>θ</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>𝐳</mi><mi>λ</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\tilde{\boldsymbol{\epsilon}}_{\theta}(\mathbf{z}_{\lambda},\mathbf{c})=(1+w)\boldsymbol{\epsilon}_{\theta}(\mathbf{z}_{\lambda},\mathbf{c})-w\boldsymbol{\epsilon}_{\theta}(\mathbf{z}_{\lambda})</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(38)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
<div id="A2.SS3.p15" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A2.SS3.p15.1" class="ltx_p">where <math id="A2.SS3.p15.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="w" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>w</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">w</annotation></semantics></math> is a hyperparameter that controls the strength of conditional guidance. This approach simplifies the training process while maintaining high controllability.</p>
</div>
<div id="A2.SS3.p16" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A2.SS3.p16.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A2.SS3.p16.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Manifold-Constrained Classifier-free Guidance</span>:  <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_cite">[<a href="#bib.bib20" title="" class="ltx_ref">20</a>]</cite> model condition generation as solving an inverse problem:</p>
</div>
<div id="A2.SS3.p17" class="ltx_para">
<table id="A2.E39" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A2.E39.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\min_{\boldsymbol{x}\in\mathcal{M}}\ell_{sds}(x),\quad\ell_{sds}(\boldsymbol{x}):=\|\boldsymbol{\epsilon}_{\theta}(\sqrt{\bar{\alpha}_{t}}\boldsymbol{x}+\sqrt{1-\bar{\alpha}_{t}}\boldsymbol{\epsilon},\boldsymbol{c})-\boldsymbol{\epsilon}\|_{2}^{2}" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><munder><mi>min</mi><mrow><mi>𝒙</mi><mo>∈</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℳ</mi></mrow></munder><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mrow><mi>s</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>d</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>s</mi></mrow></msub></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="1.167em">,</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mrow><mi>s</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>d</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>s</mi></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝒙</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>:=</mo><msubsup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mi class="ltx_mathvariant_bold-italic" mathvariant="bold-italic">ϵ</mi><mi>θ</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mrow><msqrt><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>α</mi><mo>¯</mo></mover><mi>t</mi></msub></msqrt><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>𝒙</mi></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><msqrt><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>α</mi><mo>¯</mo></mover><mi>t</mi></msub></mrow></msqrt><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi class="ltx_mathvariant_bold-italic" mathvariant="bold-italic">ϵ</mi></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo><mi>𝒄</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mi class="ltx_mathvariant_bold-italic" mathvariant="bold-italic">ϵ</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn><mn>2</mn></msubsup></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\min_{\boldsymbol{x}\in\mathcal{M}}\ell_{sds}(x),\quad\ell_{sds}(\boldsymbol{x}):=\|\boldsymbol{\epsilon}_{\theta}(\sqrt{\bar{\alpha}_{t}}\boldsymbol{x}+\sqrt{1-\bar{\alpha}_{t}}\boldsymbol{\epsilon},\boldsymbol{c})-\boldsymbol{\epsilon}\|_{2}^{2}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(39)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A2.SS3.p17.1" class="ltx_p">This implies that the goal is to identify solutions on the clean manifold <math id="A2.SS3.p17.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{M}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℳ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{M}</annotation></semantics></math> that optimally aligns with the condition <math id="A2.SS3.p17.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="c" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>c</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">c</annotation></semantics></math>.
The resulting sampling process from reverse diffusion is then given by</p>
</div>
<div id="A2.SS3.p18" class="ltx_para">
<table id="A2.E40" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A2.E40.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\begin{array}[]{rcl}x_{t-1}&amp;=&amp;\sqrt{\bar{\alpha}_{t-1}}\left(\hat{x}_{\varnothing}-\gamma_{t}\nabla_{\hat{x}_{\varnothing}}\ell_{sds}(\hat{x}_{\varnothing})\right)+\sqrt{1-\bar{\alpha}_{t-1}}\hat{\epsilon}_{\varnothing}.\end{array}" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mtable columnspacing="5pt" displaystyle="true"><mtr><mtd class="ltx_align_right" columnalign="right"><msub><mi>x</mi><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub></mtd><mtd><mo>=</mo></mtd><mtd class="ltx_align_left" columnalign="left"><mrow><mrow><mrow><msqrt><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>α</mi><mo>¯</mo></mover><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub></msqrt><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>x</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mi mathvariant="normal">∅</mi></msub><mo>−</mo><mrow><msub><mi>γ</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><msub><mo rspace="0.167em">∇</mo><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>x</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mi mathvariant="normal">∅</mi></msub></msub><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mrow><mi>s</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>d</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>s</mi></mrow></msub></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>x</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mi mathvariant="normal">∅</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><msqrt><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>α</mi><mo>¯</mo></mover><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub></mrow></msqrt><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>ϵ</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mi mathvariant="normal">∅</mi></msub></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow></mtd></mtr></mtable><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\begin{array}[]{rcl}x_{t-1}&amp;=&amp;\sqrt{\bar{\alpha}_{t-1}}\left(\hat{x}_{\varnothing}-\gamma_{t}\nabla_{\hat{x}_{\varnothing}}\ell_{sds}(\hat{x}_{\varnothing})\right)+\sqrt{1-\bar{\alpha}_{t-1}}\hat{\epsilon}_{\varnothing}.\end{array}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(40)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A2.SS3.p18.1" class="ltx_p">we can equivalently write the loss as <math id="A2.SS3.p18.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\ell_{sds}(\boldsymbol{x})=\frac{\vec{\alpha}_{t}}{1-\bar{\alpha}_{t}}\|\boldsymbol{x}-\hat{\boldsymbol{x}}_{\boldsymbol{c}}\|^{2}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mrow><mi>s</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>d</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>s</mi></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝒙</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mfrac><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>α</mi><mo stretchy="false">→</mo></mover><mi>t</mi></msub><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>α</mi><mo>¯</mo></mover><mi>t</mi></msub></mrow></mfrac><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mrow><mi>𝒙</mi><mo>−</mo><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>𝒙</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mi>𝒄</mi></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\ell_{sds}(\boldsymbol{x})=\frac{\vec{\alpha}_{t}}{1-\bar{\alpha}_{t}}\|\boldsymbol{x}-\hat{\boldsymbol{x}}_{\boldsymbol{c}}\|^{2}</annotation></semantics></math>, so it can be written as:</p>
</div>
<div id="A2.SS3.p19" class="ltx_para">
<table id="A2.E41" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A2.E41.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\boldsymbol{x}_{t-1}=\sqrt{\bar{\alpha}_{t-1}}\left(\hat{x}_{\varnothing}+\lambda(\hat{x}_{\boldsymbol{c}}-\hat{x}_{\varnothing})\right)+\sqrt{1-\bar{\alpha}_{t-1}}\hat{\boldsymbol{\epsilon}}_{\varnothing}" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>𝒙</mi><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><msqrt><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>α</mi><mo>¯</mo></mover><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub></msqrt><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>x</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mi mathvariant="normal">∅</mi></msub><mo>+</mo><mrow><mi>λ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>x</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mi>𝒄</mi></msub><mo>−</mo><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>x</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mi mathvariant="normal">∅</mi></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><msqrt><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>α</mi><mo>¯</mo></mover><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub></mrow></msqrt><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mover accent="true"><mi class="ltx_mathvariant_bold-italic" mathvariant="bold-italic">ϵ</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mi mathvariant="normal">∅</mi></msub></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\boldsymbol{x}_{t-1}=\sqrt{\bar{\alpha}_{t-1}}\left(\hat{x}_{\varnothing}+\lambda(\hat{x}_{\boldsymbol{c}}-\hat{x}_{\varnothing})\right)+\sqrt{1-\bar{\alpha}_{t-1}}\hat{\boldsymbol{\epsilon}}_{\varnothing}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(41)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
</section>
</section>
<section id="A3" class="ltx_appendix">
<h2 class="ltx_title ltx_title_appendix"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_appendix">Appendix C </span>Experiment details</h2>

<div id="A3.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A3.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A3.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Diffusion Process</span>. In all experiments, we employ a diffusion process with <math id="A3.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="T=1000" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>T</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1000</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">T=1000</annotation></semantics></math> diffusion steps, diffusion steps, parameterized by a linear schedule for <math id="A3.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\alpha_{t}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>α</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\alpha_{t}</annotation></semantics></math> and a corresponding decay for <math id="A3.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\bar{\alpha}_{\boldsymbol{t}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>α</mi><mo>¯</mo></mover><mi>𝒕</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\bar{\alpha}_{\boldsymbol{t}}</annotation></semantics></math>. For inference, we adopt the DDPM framework.</p>
</div>
<div id="A3.p2" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A3.p2.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A3.p2.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Model Architechture</span>. For the node-level task, including all node classification datasets, we use an MPNN-centric model as the encoder, which consists of GCN, GIN and GAT. Typically, we use a 5-layer architecture with residual connections and normalization layers to facilitate optimization. The optimizer is AdamW, with a learning rate of 1e-3 and a weight decay of 1e-5. The dimension of final hidden layer is set to 4. Since the node classification task only considers the node features, we only study the reconstruction loss and Riemann decoupling of the node features. Here, we initialize the curvature of a product manifold consisting of three gyroscopic space vectors with curvature -1,0,1, respectively, with dimension 4. The random Laplacian map is then calculated separately and the underlying spatial features are transformed into Riemannian Spaces. Finally, they are weighted by a linear layer and then decoded by a linear layer.</p>
</div>
<div id="A3.p3" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A3.p3.1" class="ltx_p">For graph-level tasks, such as graph generation and regression, we employ edge-enhanced graph transformers as the backbone network, incorporating position embeddings to capture structural information. For the decoder, we design a Riemannian decoupling layer for each subtask, including node-level reconstruction, edge-level reconstruction, and graph-level property reconstruction. After the Riemannian decoupling layers, a linear layer aggregates representations from each Riemannian space, and the final results are produced through an additional linear layer. The optimizer is AdamW, with a learning rate of 1e-4 and a weight decay of 1e-6. The dimension of final hidden layer is set to 16 or 32.</p>
</div>
<figure id="A3.T5" class="ltx_table">
<figcaption class="ltx_caption ltx_centering"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_table">Table 5: </span>Overview of the datasets and metrics used in the paper.</figcaption>
